-- Timbermaw Hold (map 819, the 20-man raid): the plan for the run leader (.bot run), exported from turtle-agent
-- prep/raid-tmh b0152b5 (dungeons/timbermaw_hold.json, status 'draft (not mapped, not live-checked)') with
--   turtle-agent plan-export --dir dungeons --mmaps <map 819 mmaps> --allow-draft --gm-cross-direct --approach-hops \
--     --rev b0152b5 --stamp 20261028130000 --out <this file> timbermaw_hold
-- NO ROW IS HAND-SET: the plan, leg and step rows below are the exporter's output; this header and the
-- ai_dungeon_boss block are the prep's own (task B1, ~/TortoiseBots-audit/RAID-PREP-tmh.md).
--
-- plan-check (turtle-agent plan-check --mmaps <map 819 mmaps>): ok, 270 points on the navmesh, 0 failures, 0
-- detour warnings, 82 run-leader hop notices (the approach paths below cut them), 21 patrol period estimates.
-- The draft it replaces: 287 points, 24 failing points, 134 hop notices, 2 detours.
-- The ROWS: 9 legs, 745 steps (644 move, 93 pull, 8 boss), 755 rows with the plan and leg rows.
--
-- What the prep changed from the dungeongen draft (6 legs, 150 pull groups, 275 positions, no via or approach points):
--   * 150 pull groups (275 positions) become 93 (208 units). The 28 Vile Skitterer spawns (62874, level 55, 6101 hp,
--     faction template 15: hostile_mask 0, neutral wildlife) are in every leg's skip list and in no pull. The 11 packs
--     of the z 310-364 balcony behind the Barrier of Ursol (300606, 18 units) and the 10 packs of the z 270-281 upper
--     ledge at -7500..-7370 -3590..-3370 (19 units) have no navmesh route to or from the rest of the map and are in no
--     pull (the mapping walk B2 checks whether a drop or a portal reaches them).
--   * Packs are the draft's spawn clusters merged where their units stand within 15 yd on one floor (|dz| <= 4) with a
--     server path of at most 2.2 x their distance + 8 yd, up to 12 units; radius = the pack's spread from its centre + 5,
--     at most 35 (the largest in the plan is 35, on the 11-unit satyr pack). A patrol group that stood inside a pull's
--     reach+3 is part of that pull and its patrol block moved with it (4 groups); 21 waypoint patrols carry their path and
--     an estimated period_s (the walk measures them).
--   * 9 legs by boss and floor: entrance_hall, west_ramp (Karrsh the Sentinel), rotgrowl (Kodiak first), loktanag_lower,
--     ormanos, selenaxx_foulheart, trioch_the_devourer, archdruid_kronn, chieftain_partath. The order follows the map's
--     staff list and the mesh: entrance -> Karrsh -> Rotgrowl/Kodiak -> Loktanag -> Ormanos -> Selenaxx -> Trioch ->
--     Kronn -> Partath. Karrsh (62934) and Selenaxx (62940) are boss steps though the hire unlock list does not count
--     them; Kodiak (62937) is Rotgrowl's boss.first, not a boss step.
--   * A via chain of 52 points crosses the 940-yd Rotgrowl -> Loktanag descent; the server's own path query refuses the
--     straight hop across its last 38 yd, so a 60 % point splits it. Every other leg's `to` is one server path.
--
-- WHAT THE DATA DOES NOT HAVE (nothing is invented). The core has no Timbermaw Hold instance script, and no boss but
-- Loktanag the Vile has a spell list or EventAI: the 2026-07-02 Timbermaw migration says "needs combat initialization".
--   * GOSSIP / DOORS / EVENTS: Archdruid Kronn's npc_flags 1 has no gossip_menu_id and no npc_gossip row; the four
--     braziers (300602-300605) are quest-giver game objects, the Barrier of Ursol starts open (data0 1, no script),
--     and no lever, orb, egg or altar gates the route. There is no step of any kind in this plan.
--   * URSOL 62947 and Peroth'arn 60686 have creature templates (689038 and 1201038 hp, rank 3) but no spawn row:
--     the final boss area has no data, and the secret boss needs an exalted raid member. They are not legs.
--   * Chieftain Partath (62941) and Withermaw Illuminator (62942) are faction 370 -> faction 915 (Timbermaw Hold,
--     friendly to players): without a script to turn them hostile the leg's boss cannot be attacked. The mapping walk
--     checks this first. Karrsh, Rotgrowl and Kodiak have attackable bodies and no mechanics.
--   * ai_boss_tactic: no row. Loktanag's four spells (52806 Venomous Vines, 52808 Aura of Infection, 52812 Spores of
--     Corruption, 52813 Infected Secretion) are instant (castingTimeIndex 1, interruptFlags 0), no boss has a healing
--     or buffing add, and no data names a frontal cleave or breath with a spell id. The run uses the bots' own
--     strategies; the inventory (A16) names no community patch for any Timbermaw boss.
--
-- Dungeon plans for the run leader (.bot run), exported by turtle-agent (plan-export). Plan format v1; the mapping is
-- docs/guides/dungeon-run-leader.md ("From plan v1 to rows"). The plan file in turtle-agent is the single source: edit it
-- there and export again, never these rows by hand. The plan row carries the unit lists cc_priority, cc_always and kill_first
-- (columns from 20261015200000_world.sql). Never edit this file once applied; export a new one.
--
-- Idempotent: each plan's rows are deleted, then inserted. The tables come from 20261014150000_world.sql.

-- timbermaw_hold: map 819, 9 legs, 745 steps
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_step` WHERE `plan` = 'timbermaw_hold';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_leg` WHERE `plan` = 'timbermaw_hold';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_plan` WHERE `plan` = 'timbermaw_hold';

-- The eight bosses of the plan's boss steps (map 819), for the boss rank and the dashboard: a DELETE of this map and
-- these entries, then REPLACE. Kodiak 62937 is Rotgrowl's boss.first add, so it is not seeded.
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_boss` WHERE `map` IN (819) AND `entry` IN (2139, 62934, 62935, 62936, 62938, 62940, 62941, 62946);
